<title>MEXICO: Mexico hog population estimated at 14 mln head.</title>
<headline>Mexico hog population estimated at 14 mln head.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's hog population is estimated at around 14 million head, specialist veterinarians Laboratorios Columbia said in a document obtained Wednesday.</p>
<p>Columbia said it calculated that 190 fully-automated modern farms had an inventory of 4.48 million head, 1,875 semi-automated farms had 3.92 million and an unknown number of unautomated farms had 5.6 million.</p>
<p>Colombia, outlining its estimates in the Mexican Hog Farming Council's magazine, said Jalisco was the top producer state with 14.7 percent of the total. Sonora was second with 8.3 percent, Chiapas had 8.0 percent, and Veracruz, Puebla and Michoacan all with a tad more than 7.0 percent.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
